# Pixhawk outputs for firmware/VCB-pixhawk (reversible VCB build, 1500 us = stop).
# DO NOT apply while the deployed forward-only VCB build is flashed: it reads 1500 us
# as 50 % thrust (clamped to 20 %) on both motors as soon as it arms.
# Apply with tools/ap_apply.py params/vcb-pixhawk.parm after flashing and after the
# bench check in firmware/VCB-pixhawk/README.md. Overrides the SERVO9/10 lines in boat.parm.
#
# Functions unchanged: AUX1 -> VCB ch1 (right), AUX2 -> VCB ch2 (left), measured 2026-10-04.
SERVO9_FUNCTION,74
SERVO10_FUNCTION,73
# VCB: 25 us deadband around 1500, then (|us-1500| - 25) * 1000/475 permille, applied =
# clamp(raw, -THRUST_LIMIT_PERMILLE, +THRUST_LIMIT_PERMILLE). 2026-11-08 with VCB 0.3.3: the
# Pixhawk outputs the full 1000..2000 us and the VCB's 600 permille (60 %) clamp is the only
# thrust limit; 60 % is reached at 1810 / 1190 us, Rover throttle beyond ~62 % is flat.
# (0.3.2 and earlier: 1380/1620 = the 20 % band.) DO NOT apply with 0.3.2 or older flashed
# and expect more thrust: that firmware still clamps at 20 %.
# TRIM 1500 = stop, also the disarmed output, which is what arms the VCB.
SERVO9_MIN,1000
SERVO9_TRIM,1500
SERVO9_MAX,2000
SERVO10_MIN,1000
SERVO10_TRIM,1500
SERVO10_MAX,2000
#
# RC switches on the RadioMaster Boxer (ELRS XR3 on TELEM2, SERIAL2_PROTOCOL 23), set 2026-11-03.
# Switch sense as chosen on the Boxer 2026-11-03, with the switches left in the disarm /
# e-stop position the whole time: Pixhawk reads RC5 999 and RC8 987 there. Option 153 arms on
# logical high, so RC5 is not reversed (999 = disarm, 2000 = arm). Option 31 stops on logical
# high, so RC8 is reversed (987 = motor emergency stop, 2011 = cleared); RC_OPTIONS bit 7
# makes REVERSED apply to switches. Verified live: 'PreArm: Motors Emergency Stopped' with
# the switches untouched. E-stop forces AUX1/AUX2 to 1500 us, VCB sees cmd 0. Arm/disarm
# fires on switch movement, not on boot.
RC5_OPTION,153
RC5_REVERSED,0
RC8_OPTION,31
RC8_REVERSED,1
RC_OPTIONS,8352     # 32 throttle-neutral arming check + 128 switch reverse + 8192 ELRS 420 kbaud
# Applied 2026-11-08 on the boat (pre-arm blockers for RC in Manual; one reboot):
RC3_TRIM,1500        # throttle is spring-centred; Rover treats throttle as an angle about TRIM
ARMING_RUDDER,0      # no stick arming on a boat; RC5 is the only arm path
COMPASS_ENABLE,0     # internal BMM150 only, uncalibrated; yaw comes from the UM982 (EK3_SRC1_YAW 2)
COMPASS_USE,0
BATT_MONITOR,0       # PM02D never healthy; pack is read by the Jetson from the LiTime BMS
# UM982 baseline, measured 2026-11-08: ANT1 on the transom, ANT2 forward on the centreline,
# 12.5 ft = 3.81 m, no significant Y/Z or yaw offset. First fit read ~157 deg with the bow
# near north (cables swapped); after swapping ANT1/ANT2 at the receiver it reads close to
# the bow. Heading with no compass now depends on the UM982's heading solution.
GPS1_MB_OFS_X,3.81
GPS1_MB_OFS_Y,0
GPS1_MB_OFS_Z,0
# Still pending: only once QGC shows no PreArm messages after the reboot above.
#ARMING_SKIPCHK,0    # was 64 (RC checks skipped); RC is calibrated now
